      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a concise Quick Start guide for the NebulaFlow CLI tool:\n\n**Quick Start Guide: Deploying with NebulaFlow CLI**\n\nTo get started with NebulaFlow, follow these simple steps:\n\n1. **Log In**: Use the NebulaFlow CLI to authenticate by running `nf auth login --token <TOKEN>`. Replace `<TOKEN>` with your active NebulaFlow token.\n2. **Initialize a Cluster**: Create a new cluster by running `nf cluster init`, specifying the desired region (`--region us-east-1`) and shard size (`--size small`).\n\nExample:\n```bash\nnf cluster init --region us-east-1 --size small\n```\n3. **Deploy Your Application**: Configure your deployment settings using a YAML file (`./production.yaml`) and deploy your application by running `nf deploy`.\n\nExample:\n```bash\nnf deploy --config ./production.yaml\n```\nThat's it! Your NebulaFlow cluster is now up and running. Make sure to adjust the deployment settings and token as needed for your specific use case.",
